        },
        {
          "start": 55,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "use, and easy to also implement really kind of&nbsp; general solutions to general problems with the&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 60,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "off the shelf models that are already available&nbsp; to you. I'm going to walk you through in part one&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 65,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "of this video series how to get the most out&nbsp; of spacey with these off the shelf features.&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 70,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "In part two, we're going to start tackling some&nbsp; of the features that don't exist in off the shelf&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 75,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "models. And I'm going to show you how to use rules&nbsp; based pipes or components in spacey to actually&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 80,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "sole domain specific problems and your own area&nbsp; from the entity ruler to the matcher to actually&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 85,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "injecting robust complex regular expression or&nbsp; regex patterns, and a custom spacey component&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 90,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "that doesn't actually exist at the moment. I'm&nbsp; going to be showing you all that in part two,&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 95,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "so that in part three, we can take the lessons&nbsp; that we learned in part one and part two, and&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 100,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "actually apply them to solve a very kind of common&nbsp; problem that exists in NLP and that is information&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 105,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "extraction from financial documents. So finding&nbsp; things that are of relevance, such as stocks,&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 110,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "markets, indexes and stock exchanges. If you join&nbsp; me over the next few hours, you will leave this&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 115,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "lesson with a good understanding of the standing&nbsp; of spacey and also a good understanding of kind&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 120,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "of the off the shelf components that are there&nbsp; and a way to take the off the shelf components&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 125,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "and apply them to your own domain. If you also&nbsp; join me in this video and you like it, please let&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 130,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "me know in the comments down below because I am&nbsp; interested in making a second part to this video&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 135,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "that will explore not only the rules based aspects&nbsp; of spacey, but the machine learning based aspects&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 140,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "of spacey. So teaching you how to train your&nbsp; own models to do your own things such as&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 145,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "training a dependency parser, training a named&nbsp; entity recognizer things like this, which are not&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 150,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "covered in this video. Nevertheless, if you join&nbsp; me for this one and you like it, you will find&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 155,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "part two, much easier to understand. So sit back,&nbsp; relax, and let's jump into what NLP is, what kind&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 160,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "of things you can do with NLP such as information&nbsp; extraction, and what the spacey library is and how&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 165,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "this course will be laid out. If you like this&nbsp; video, also consider subscribing to my channel&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 170,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "Python tutorials for digital humanities,&nbsp; which is linked in the description down below.&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 175,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "Even if you're not a digital humanists like&nbsp; me, you will find these Python tutorials useful&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 180,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "because they take Python and make it accessible&nbsp; to students of all levels. specifically those who&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 185,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "are beginners, I walk you through not only the&nbsp; basics of Python, but also I walk you through&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 190,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "step by step some of the more common libraries&nbsp; that you need. A lot of the channel deals with&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 195,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "texts or text based problems. But other content&nbsp; deals with things like machine learning, and&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 200,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "image classification and OCR, all in Python. So&nbsp; before we begin with spacey, I think we should&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 205,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "spend a little bit of time talking about what&nbsp; NLP or natural language processing actually is.&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 210,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "Natural Language Processing is the process&nbsp; by which we try to get a computer system&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 215,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "to understand and parse and extract human language&nbsp; oftentimes with raw text. There are a couple&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 220,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "different areas of natural language processing.&nbsp; There's named entity recognition, part of speech&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 225,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "tagging, syntactic parsing, text categorization,&nbsp; also known as text classification, co reference&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 230,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "resolution machine translation. Adjacent to NLP&nbsp; is another kind of computational linguistics field&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 235,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "called natural language understanding NLU&nbsp; This is where we train computer systems to&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 240,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "do things like relation extraction, semantic&nbsp; parsing, question and answering this is where&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 245,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "bots really kind of come into play, summarization,&nbsp; sentiment analysis and paraphrasing. NLP and NLU&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 250,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "are used by a wide array of industries, from&nbsp; finance industry, all the way through to law&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 255,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "and academia with researchers trying to do&nbsp; information extraction from texts. Within an LP,&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 260,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "there's a couple different applications. The first&nbsp; and probably the most important is information&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 265,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "extraction. This is the process by which we try to&nbsp; get a computer system to extract information that&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 270,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "we find relevant to our own research or needs. So&nbsp; for example, as we're gonna see, in part three of&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 275,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "this video, when we need to apply spacey to the&nbsp; financial sector, a person interested in finances&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 280,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "might need an LP to go through and extract things&nbsp; like company names, stocks, indexes, things that&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 285,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "are referenced within maybe news articles, from&nbsp; Reuters to New York Times to Wall Street Journal.&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 290,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "This is an example of using NLP to extract&nbsp; information. A good way to think about NLP&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 295,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "is application in this area, is it takes in some&nbsp; unstructured data, in this case, raw text, and&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 300,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "extracts structured data from it or metadata. So&nbsp; it finds the things that you want it to find and&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 305,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "extracts them for you. Now while there's ways to&nbsp; do this with gazetteers, and list matching, using&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 310,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "an NLP framework, like spacey, which I'll talk&nbsp; about in just a second, has certain advantages,&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 315,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "the main one being that you can use and leverage&nbsp; things that have been parsed syntactically or&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 320,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "semantically. So things like the part of speech of&nbsp; a word things like its dependencies, things like&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 325,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "its co reference, these are things that the spacey&nbsp; framework allow for you to do off the shelf,&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 330,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "and also train into machine learning models, and&nbsp; work into pipelines with rules. So that's kind of&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 335,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "one aspect of NLP. And one way it's used. Another&nbsp; way it's used is to read in data and classify it.&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 340,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "This is known as text categorization. And we&nbsp; see that on the left hand side of this image,&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 345,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "text categorization or text classification. And we&nbsp; conclude in this sentiment analysis for the most&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 350,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "part as well, is a way we take information into&nbsp; a computer system, again, unstructured data or&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 355,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "raw text, and we classify it in some way. you've&nbsp; actually seen this at work for many decades now,&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 360,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "with spam detection, spam detection is nearly&nbsp; perfect, it needs to be continually updated.&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 365,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "But for the most part, it is a solved problem. The&nbsp; reason why you have emails that automatically go&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 370,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "to your spam folder, is because there's a machine&nbsp; learning model that sits on the background of&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 375,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "your on the back end of your email server. And&nbsp; what it does is it actually looks at the emails,&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 380,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "it sees if it fat fits the pattern for what it's&nbsp; seen as spam before, and it assigns it a spam&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 385,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "label. This is known as classification. This is&nbsp; also used by researchers, especially in the legal&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 390,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "industry, lawyers oftentimes receive hundreds of&nbsp; 1000s of documents, if not millions of documents,&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 395,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "they don't necessarily have the human time to&nbsp; go through and analyze every single document&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 400,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "verbatim. It is important to kind of get a quick&nbsp; umbrella sense of the documents without actually&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 405,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "having to go through and read them page by&nbsp; page. And so what lawyers will oftentimes do&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 410,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "is use NLP to do classification and information&nbsp; extraction, they will find keywords that are&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 415,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "relevant to their case, or they will find&nbsp; documents that are classified according to the&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 420,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "relevant fields of their case. And that way, they&nbsp; can take a million documents and reduce it down&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 425,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "to maybe only a handful, maybe 1000 that they have&nbsp; to read verbatim. This is a real world application&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 430,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "of NLP or natural language processing. And&nbsp; both of these tasks can be achieved through&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 435,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "the spacey framework. spacey is a framework&nbsp; for doing NLP right now. As of 2021, it's only&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 440,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "available I believe in Python, I think there is a&nbsp; community that's working on an application with R&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 445,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "but I don't know that for certain. But spacey&nbsp; is one of many NLP frameworks that Python has&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 450,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "available. If you're interested in looking at all&nbsp; of them, you can explore things like NLT Kay, the&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 455,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "natural language toolkit stanza, which I believe&nbsp; is coming out of the same program at Stanford.&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 460,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "There's many out there, but I find spacey to be&nbsp; the best of all of them for a couple different&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 465,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "reasons. Reason one is that they provide for you&nbsp; off the shelf models that benchmark very well&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 470,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "meaning they perform very quickly. And they also&nbsp; have very good accuracy metrics such as precision&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 475,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "recall, and F score. And I'm not going to talk&nbsp; too much about the way we measure machine learning&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 480,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "accuracy right now, but know that they are quite&nbsp; good. Second, spacey has the ability to leverage&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 485,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "current natural language processing methods,&nbsp; specifically transformer models, also known,&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 490,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "usually kind of collectively as Bert models, even&nbsp; though that's not entirely accurate, but it allows&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 495,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "for you to use an off the shelf transformer&nbsp; model. And third, it provides the framework for&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 500,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "doing custom training relatively easily compared&nbsp; to these other NLP frameworks that are out there.&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 505,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "Finally, the fourth reason why I picked spacey&nbsp; over other NLP frameworks is because it scales&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 510,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "well. spacey was designed by explosion AI, and the&nbsp; entire Purpose of spacey is to work at scale AI&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 515,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "at scale, we mean working with large quantities of&nbsp; documents efficiently, effectively and accurately.&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 520,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "spacey scales well because it can process hundreds&nbsp; of 1000s of documents with relative ease in&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 525,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "a relatively short period of time, especially if&nbsp; you stick with more rules based pipes, which we're&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 530,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "going to talk about in part two of this video. So&nbsp; those are the two things you really need to know&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 535,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "about NLP, and spacey in general, we're going to&nbsp; talk about spacey in depth as we explore it both&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 540,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "through this video. And and the free textbook&nbsp; I provide to go along with this video, which is&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 545,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "located at spacey dot python humanities.com. And&nbsp; it should be linked in the description down below&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 550,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "this video and the textbook I meant to work in&nbsp; tandem. Some stuff that I cover in the video&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 555,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "might not necessarily be in the textbook&nbsp; because it doesn't lend itself well to&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 560,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "text representation. And the same goes for the&nbsp; opposite some stuff that I don't have the time&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 565,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "to cover verbatim In this video, I cover&nbsp; in a little bit more depth in the video.&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 570,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "And in the book, I think that you should try&nbsp; to use both of these, what I would recommend&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 575,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "is doing one pass through this whole video, watch&nbsp; it in its entirety and get an umbrella sense of&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 580,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "everything that space you can do. And everything&nbsp; that we're going to cover, I would then go back&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 585,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "and try to replicate each stage of this process on&nbsp; a separate window or on a separate screen and try&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 590,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "to kind of follow along and code and then I would&nbsp; go back through a third time and try to watch the&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 595,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "first part Why talk about what we're going to be&nbsp; doing and try to do it on your own without looking&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 600,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "at the textbook or the video. If you can do that&nbsp; by your third pass, you'll be in very good shape&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 605,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "to start using spacey to solve your own domain&nbsp; specific problems. NLP is a complex field and&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 610,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "applying NLP is really complex. But fortunately,&nbsp; frameworks like spacey make this project and this&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 615,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "process a lot easier. I encourage you to spend a&nbsp; few hours in this video get to know spacey and I&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 620,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "think you're going to find that you can do things&nbsp; that you didn't think possible and relatively&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 625,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "short order. So sit back, relax and enjoy this&nbsp; video series on spacey. In order to use spacey,&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 630,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "you're first going to have to install spacey. Now&nbsp; there's a few different ways to do this. Depending&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 635,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "on your environment and your operating system,&nbsp; I recommend going to spacey.io backslash usage&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 640,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "and kind of enter in the correct framework that&nbsp; you're working with. So if you're using Mac OS&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 645,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "versus windows versus Linux, you can go through&nbsp; and in this very handy kind of user interface, you&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 650,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "can go through and select the different features&nbsp; that matter most to you. I'm working with Windows,&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 655,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "I'm going to be using PIP in this case, and&nbsp; I'm going to be doing everything on the CPU.&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 660,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "And I'm going to be working with English. So I've&nbsp; established all of those different parameters.&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 665,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "And it goes through and it tells me exactly&nbsp; how to go through and install it using PIP&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 670,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "in the terminal. So I encourage you to&nbsp; go through and pause the video right now&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 675,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "go ahead and install Windows however you want to.&nbsp; I'm going to be walking through how to install it&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 680,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "within the Jupyter Notebook that we're going to&nbsp; be moving to in just a second. I want you to not&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 685,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "work with the GPU at all. Working with spacey on&nbsp; the GPU requires a lot more understanding about&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 690,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "what the GPU is used for specifically, in training&nbsp; machine learning models. It requires you to have&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 695,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "CUDA installed correctly. It requires a&nbsp; couple other things that I don't really&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 700,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "have the time to get into in this video, but we'll&nbsp; be addressing in a more advanced spacey tutorial&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 705,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "video. So for right now, I recommend selecting&nbsp; your o s selecting either can use PIP or conda&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 710,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "and then selecting CPU. And since you're going to&nbsp; be working through this video with English texts,&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 715,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "I encourage you to select English right now&nbsp; and go ahead and just install or download&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 720,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "the N core web SM model. This is the small&nbsp; model. I'll talk about that in just a second.&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 725,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "So the first thing we're going to do in our&nbsp; Jupyter Notebook is we're going to be using the&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 730,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "the exclamation mark to delineate in the cell that&nbsp; this is a terminal command, we're going to say pip&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 735,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "install spacey, your output when you execute&nbsp; this cell is going to look a little different&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 740,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "than mine. I already have spacey installed in this&nbsp; environment. And so mind kind of goes through and&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 745,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "looks like this yours will actually go through and&nbsp; instead of saying requirement already satisfied&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 750,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "it'll be actually passing out the the different&nbsp; things that it's actually installing to install&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 755,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "spacey and all of its dependencies. The next thing&nbsp; that you're going to do is you're going to again,&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 760,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "you follow the instructions, and you're&nbsp; going to be doing Python dash m space spacey,&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 765,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "space download, and then the model that you want&nbsp; to download. So let's go ahead and do that right&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 770,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "now. So let's go ahead and say Python m spacing.&nbsp; Download to this is a spacey terminal command.&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 775,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "And we're going to download the N core web SM&nbsp; and again, I already have this model downloaded&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 780,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "So on my end, spacey is going to look a&nbsp; little differently than as it's going to&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 785,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "look on your end as it prints off on the Jupyter&nbsp; Notebook. And if we give it a just a second,&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 790,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "everything will go through, and it says that&nbsp; it's collected it, it's downloading it. And we&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 795,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "are all very happy now. And so now that we've got&nbsp; spacey installed correctly, and that we've got the&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 800,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "small model downloaded correctly, we can go ahead&nbsp; and start actually using spacey and make sure&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 805,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "everything's correct. The first thing we're going&nbsp; to do is we're going to import the spacey library&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 810,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "as you would with any other Python library. If&nbsp; you're not familiar with this, a library is simply&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 815,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "a set of classes and functions that you can import&nbsp; into a Python script so that you don't have to&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 820,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "write a whole bunch of extra code. Libraries&nbsp; are massive collections of classes and functions&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 825,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "that you can call. So when we import spacey,&nbsp; we're importing the whole library of spacey&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 830,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "and now that we've seen something like this,&nbsp; we know that spacey has imported correctly,&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 835,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "as long as you're not getting an error message,&nbsp; everything was in was imported fine. The next&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 840,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "thing that we need to do is we want to make sure&nbsp; that our English core web SM are small English&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 845,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "model was downloaded correctly. So the next thing&nbsp; that we need to do is we need to create an NLP&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 850,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "object. I'm going to be talking a lot more about&nbsp; this as we move forward. Right now, this is just&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 855,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "troubleshooting to make sure that we've installed&nbsp; spacey correctly and we've downloaded our model&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 860,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "correctly. So we're going to use the spacey dot&nbsp; load command. This is going to take one argument,&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 865,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "it's going to be a string that is going to&nbsp; correspond to the model that you've installed.&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 870,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "And this case n cor web s n. And if you&nbsp; execute this cell and you have no errors,&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 875,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "you have successfully installed spacey correctly&nbsp; and you've downloaded the English core web SM&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 880,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "model correctly. So go ahead take time, and get&nbsp; all this stuff set up. Pause the video if you need&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 885,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "to, and then pop back and we're going to start&nbsp; actually working through the basics of spacey.&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 890,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "I'm now going to move into kind of an&nbsp; overview of kind of what's within spacey,&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 895,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "why it's useful and kind of some of the basic&nbsp; features of it that you need to be familiar with.&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 900,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "And I'm going to be working from the Jupyter&nbsp; Notebook that I talked about and the introduction&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 905,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "to this video. If we scroll down to the bottom of&nbsp; chapter one, the basics of spacey, then you get&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 910,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "past the install section, you get to this section&nbsp; on containers. So what are containers? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 915,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "containers within spacey are objects that&nbsp; contain a large quantity of data about a text.&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 920,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "There are several different containers that&nbsp; you can work with. In spacey, there's the doc,&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 925,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "the doc Ben example, language,&nbsp; lexeme span, span group and token,&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 930,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "we're going to be dealing with the lexeme a&nbsp; little bit in this video series. And we're&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 935,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "going to be dealing with the language container&nbsp; a little bit in this video series. But really,&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 940,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "the three big things that we're going to be&nbsp; talking about again and again is the dock&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 945,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "the span and the token. And I think when you&nbsp; first come to spacey, there's a little bit of&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 950,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "a learning curve about what these things are, what&nbsp; they do, how they are structured hierarchically.&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 955,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "And for that reason I've created this,&nbsp; in my opinion, kind of easy to understand&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 960,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "image of what different containers are. So if&nbsp; you think about what spacey is as a pyramid,&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 965,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "so a hierarchical system, we've got all&nbsp; these different containers structured around,&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 970,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "really the dock object, your Docker container,&nbsp; or your dock object contains a whole bunch of&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 975,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "metadata about the text that you pass to the&nbsp; spacey pipeline, which we're going to see&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 980,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "in practice, and just a few minutes. The doc&nbsp; object contains a bunch of different things.&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 985,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "It contains attributes. And these attributes&nbsp; can be things like, like sentences. So if you&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 990,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "iterate over doc dot cents, you can actually&nbsp; access all the different sentences found within&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 995,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "that doc object. If you iterate over each&nbsp; individual item, or index and your doc object,&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1000,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "you can get individual tokens. tokens are going&nbsp; to be things like words or punctuation marks&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1005,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "something within your sentence or text&nbsp; that has a self contained important value,&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1010,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "either syntactically or semantically. So this&nbsp; is going to be things like words a comma period,&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1015,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "a semi colon, a quotation mark, things like this,&nbsp; these are all going to be your tokens. And we're&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1020,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "going to see how tokens are a little different&nbsp; than just splitting words up with traditional&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1025,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "string methods and Python. The next thing that&nbsp; you should be kind of familiar with are spans.&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1030,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "So spans are important because they kind of exist&nbsp; within and without of the doc object. So unlike&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1035,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "the token, which is an index of the doc object,&nbsp; a span can be a token itself, but it can also&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1040,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "be a sequence of multiple tokens, we're gonna see&nbsp; that at play. So imagine if you had a span in its&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1045,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "category, maybe group one are our places. So a&nbsp; single token might be like a city like Berlin,&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1050,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "but span group two, this could be something like&nbsp; full proper names. So of people, for example. So&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1055,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "this could be like, as we're going to see Martin&nbsp; Luther King, this would be a sequence of tokens, a&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1060,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "sequence of three different items in the sentence&nbsp; that make up one span, or one self contained item.&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1065,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "So Martin Luther King, would be a person who's&nbsp; a collection of a sequence of individual tokens.&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1070,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "If that doesn't make sense, right now, this&nbsp; image will be reinforced as we go through&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1075,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "and learn more about spacey in practice. For&nbsp; right now, I want you to be just understanding&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1080,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "that the doc object is the thing around which&nbsp; all of spacey sits, this is going to be the&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1085,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "object that you create. This is going to be the&nbsp; object that contains all the metadata that you&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1090,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "need to access. And this is going to be the&nbsp; object that you tried to essentially improve&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1095,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "with different custom components, factories, and&nbsp; pipelines. As you go through and do more advanced&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1100,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "things with spacey, we're going to now see in&nbsp; just a few seconds how that dock object is kind&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1105,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "of similar to the text itself. But how it's&nbsp; very, very different and much more powerful.&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1110,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "We're now going to be moving on to chapter two&nbsp; of this textbook, which is going to deal with&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1115,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "kind of getting used to the in depth features&nbsp; of spacing. If you want to pause the video or&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1120,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "keep this notebook or this book open up to&nbsp; kind of separate from this video and follow&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1125,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "along. As we go through and explore it in live&nbsp; coding, we're going to be talking about a few&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1130,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "different things as we explore chapter two,&nbsp; this will be a lot longer than chapter one,&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1135,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "we're going to be not only importing spacey, but&nbsp; actually going through and loading up a model,&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1140,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "creating a dog object around that model. So that&nbsp; we're going to work with container and practice.&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1145,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "And then we're going to see how that container&nbsp; stores a lot of different features or metadata&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1150,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "attributes about the text. And while&nbsp; they look the same on the surface,&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1155,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "they're actually quite different. So let's&nbsp; go ahead and work within our same Jupyter&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1160,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "Notebook where we've imported spacey and we have&nbsp; already created the NLP object. The first thing&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1165,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "that I want to do is I want to open up a text to&nbsp; start working with within this repo, we've got&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1170,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "a data folder. Within this data sub folder,&nbsp; I've got a couple different Wikipedia openings,&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1175,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "I've got one on MLK that we're going to be using&nbsp; a little later in this video. And then I have one&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1180,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "on the United States, this is wiki underscore us.&nbsp; That's going to be what we work with right now.&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1185,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "So let's use our width operator and open up&nbsp; the data backslash wiki underscore us dot txt.&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1190,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "We're gonna just read that in as F. And then we're&nbsp; going to create this text object which is going to&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1195,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "be equal to F dot read. And now that we've got&nbsp; our text object created, let's go ahead and see&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1200,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "what this looks like. So let's print text. And&nbsp; we see that it's a standard Wikipedia article&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1205,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "kind of follows that same introductory format and&nbsp; it's about four or five paragraphs long with a&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1210,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "lot of the features left in such as the brackets&nbsp; that delineate some kind of a footnote. We're not&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1215,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "going to worry too much about cleaning this up&nbsp; right now, because we're interested in not with&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1220,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "cleaning our data so much as just starting&nbsp; to work with the doc object in spacey.&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "start": 1225,
          "duration": 5,
          "text": "So the first thing that you want to do is&nbsp; you're going to want to create a doc object"
        }
